@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+# Faster repeated race entry — 2 November 2026
+
+The first three recommendations from the [loading evaluation](RACE_LOADING_REVIEW_2026_11_02.md) are implemented locally: bounded effect draws, useful scenery retention within the existing memory allowance, and earlier selected-track CPU preparation. No car, terrain, shader, texture, visual-quality setting, camera, handling or backend contract changes are made.
+
+## Measured result
+
+An interleaved offline actual-App Star/Pine fixture compared the task-start effect loop and memory policy with the new policies in the same process. Both paths use current geometry/rendering and retain the final full covered draw. The private profiles use Godot 4.7.2, Windows, RTX 3090, 1280×720 and Dummy audio. After startup, engine time is frozen for stable images and tick-zero loading observations. Driver/OS caches are not erased; the host is shared. This is a warm desktop re-entry experiment, not a cold-driver, packaged-build or Android result.
+
+| Renderer | Warm control samples | Optimized retained-world samples | Median reduction |
+| --- | --- | --- | ---: |
+| Compatibility | 1,231.790 / 1,273.798 / 1,317.334 ms | 508.748 / 497.366 ms | 60.51% |
+| Desktop Mobile | 2,109.850 / 1,957.707 / 1,747.385 ms | 700.775 / 754.065 ms | 62.84% |
+
+The optimized pairs first populate their scenery cache, then consume it. Cycles 2/6 are those population entries, not included in the retained-world column: 984.944/1,037.728 ms Compatibility and 1,563.702/1,314.483 ms Mobile. Cold process seeds, all eight rows per renderer, pre-entry cache state, preparation stages and largest frame are retained in the raw evidence. Controls intentionally use the previous policy, so neither control can retain its scenery between entries. These small samples do not establish a general percentage gain.
+
+Each renderer saved eight native frames. All seven post-seed frames within each renderer are byte-identical PNG files, including the optimized frames and later restored controls: **12 independent exact comparisons** against the first warm control. Mobile's initial procedural-car seed differs from every later warm frame in seven channel bytes by 1/255; subsequent control and optimized images match exactly. Both control and optimized loading states keep tick zero, the complete countdown and five laps. The interleaved runs each pass **21 checks / 0 failures**, with stable recorded source hashes within each run.
+
+The four effect/cache implementation sources are unchanged from those measurements. Selected CPU priming was subsequently refined to avoid constructing a discarded bridge/Desert field or rebaking Winter cover; the final CPU path is checked separately. The benchmark bypasses normal selection dwell and does not measure that scheduling benefit. Severe first-use shader/driver work is **not fixed** by this task; removing covered draws or changing the renderer is not part of the implementation.
+
+## Implementation
+
+- **RLX01 — effect preparation:** `game/vehicle/effect_render_preparation.gd` draws up to four reused GPU proxies per covered interval. Fresh nodes retain individual first draws. Every actual source still supplies its own process material, meshes and render settings and is drawn, including when those properties change; there is no inferred shader/pipeline-equivalence shortcut and no recursive serialization key. Cancellation is checked at each bounded draw; only completed batches can return initialized leases. The final full covered frame remains. The existing all-theme bridge fixture observes 28 fresh Pine proxies in 28 draws, then the same 28 retained proxies in seven draws. Winter's bounded pool retains 36/40 nodes and needs 13 draws on repeat, preserving the four required fresh draws.
+- **RLX02 — shared scenery retention:** `game/track/prepared_world_cache.gd` records the immutable mesh identities/costs actually owned by its detached cached copies, including bounded map overhead. `game/editor/editor_memory.gd` subtracts only exact road/world mesh aliases from its combined estimate. Equal arrays in distinct resources do not qualify; nodes and mutable MultiMesh buffers remain independently accounted. Ordinary budget arbitration can evict idle preparation proxies before discarding a completed world. The total 64 MiB allowance, world/road limits and 12 MiB/64-node proxy limits are unchanged. A trim generation also prevents a cooperative snapshot from republishing optional scenery after pressure. Star's example counts 28,245,312 shared stream bytes once and retains its completed world at 61,040,228 estimated bytes after arbitration; these are conservative ownership estimates, not measured GPU allocation or Android PSS.
+- **RLX03 — selected CPU preparation:** `game/race/selected_track_preparation.gd` primes the existing query, bounded numeric support cache and canonical checkpoint layout in the same already-owned selection worker, after roads/cover preparation. It publishes no additional presenter or track owner. `game/core/app.gd` allows a selected track with warm roads but missing/currently obsolete gate layout to receive that work, waiting for retiring jobs before reading layout readiness. Existing account, selection, car, revision, navigation, cancellation and hydration fences remain. Race authorization/ticket issuance is not moved. The layout is exactly equal to the original constructor's data; no simulation or rule version changes are needed.
+
+Proxy retention and scenery retention compete within the same allowance. In the full Star example, budget arbitration keeps six of twenty idle proxies so it can preserve the more valuable completed world; the next entry redraws the other fourteen individually. The policy does not assume that every warm race receives the component fixture's four-to-one batching benefit, and it does not raise memory limits to obtain the speedup.
+
+## Validation and retained findings
+
+The focused ownership/budget/CPU regression passes **20/0** on final sources. It covers exact resource identity, distinct equal geometry, actual cached-scene ownership, preserved active geometry, unchanged combined allowance, ordinary proxy eviction, real pressure suppression, pressure during cooperative snapshotting, exact gate data and cancelled jobs. The existing native fitting/effect/lifetime suite passes **622/0 on each renderer**, retaining its task-start front geometry/shader fingerprints, all five themes including bridge effects, live-source state, node/resource bounds, reuse, cancellation, pressure and teardown.
+
+The earlier actual-App loading-reuse regression passes **526/0** in its recorded headless run. A final rerun on the concurrently updated App records **630/0 assertions but an engine error at shutdown**: `garage_opening_showroom.gd:50` resumes `_begin_studio` after its instance is gone. It is not a clean pass. The same current-App test with the task-start effect loop, memory policy and selected worker records **648/0 assertions and the identical Garage engine error**. Concurrent App startup/Garage/music edits are preserved and excluded from this task's checkpoint; the five recorded race-loading functions remain unchanged. The two raw controls are retained, and this Garage shutdown issue remains unresolved in its concurrent code. Two older suites also retain specific failures rather than weakening their assertions:
+
+- Selected preparation: **59 checks / 1 failure**, requiring an installed `.res` to replace numeric `.arrays`. The unchanged-assertion task-start selected-worker control produces the identical failure and passes its other fences. The current cooperative loader intentionally retains a valid numeric road artifact; its existing write condition does not replace it with a GPU resource artifact on this path. No disk-format behavior is changed here.
+- Prepared-world suite: **85 checks / 1 failure**, expecting a deleted source document to bypass an existing retained-document fallback. Its geometry, material, transform, mutable-instance and budget assertions across all five biomes pass. A cloud-only control using the task-start world-cache class fails the identical assertion (**10/1**) before building or restoring any world. Cloud/cache backend sources are unchanged by this task.
+
+The native driving fixture uses the existing locally stored `backend/tests/fixtures/verified_oval.json`. All five biome opening laps complete with zero contacts on both desktop renderers. The full final Mobile integration run passes **135/0**, including every current car, first real emissions, tick-zero reveal, cancellation/account/car/selection fences, pressure and teardown. Concurrent edits changed App on disk during that run; this is not a whole-tree source freeze, while the recorded race-function scope remains unchanged. Its first real emissions require no new draw pipelines. Compatibility's preceding full run records five valid laps but reports six fixture-only cancellation-observation failures: it queried visibility after Game had already been freed. The corrected focused cancellation/pressure/teardown rerun passes **31/0**; none of those six failures involved a race or material change. Both full-run evidence and correction are retained.
+
+Driving-frame intervals remain observations, not a 60 FPS guarantee. Compatibility records a roughly 214 ms Night frame; its pipeline counter cannot establish native GL compilation behavior. Mobile records one new draw pipeline during the Desert lap, after the separately passing first-emission check. The same verified Desert case with the task-start effect loop and memory policy also records one new draw pipeline, completes its lap with zero contacts and passes **13/0**. Other Mobile biome laps report zero new draw pipelines. The implementation claims reduced loading work, not elimination of all first-lap or driver hitches.
+
+A read-only inspection of twenty prepared modular car scenes finds no newly invalidated previously eligible template from this task: all twenty already fail their task-start source/key guards because of earlier model revisions. They retain their safe procedural fallback. No stale model is blessed and no unrelated model/template/art assets or generated build identity are refreshed.
+
+Initial attempts are preserved: a restricted headless run reports log/certificate-store access errors; the diagnostic control wrapper initially used inconsistent indentation; an initial benchmark called an unavailable shader-time API and was corrected to the documented engine time scale; a control's overly broad preload anchor was corrected to match exact declarations. The original native ellipse left the AI with zero completed laps and 9,239 contacts after 90 seconds. That owned test tree was stopped, its logs retained, and the established verified oval replaced the unsuitable driving fixture. Hover's intentionally hidden tyre effects and post-cancellation lifetime expectations were corrected in the test fixture; complete visible-source coverage, bounds and freeze assertions remain. No runtime AI/handling changes are made.
+
+## Reproduction and scope
+
+All final commands use [the bounded runner](evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/run_check.py), which invokes the pinned executable under `scripts/run_no_crash_dialog.py`. Profiles, records, libraries, cloud folders and road caches are task-owned. The final runner also writes an explicit empty private backend configuration to avoid the Windows empty-environment fallback; initial probes used the empty API environment and offline race starts. No real session, purchase, authenticated/live backend write, deployment, APK/export, device query/test, owner-save modification, owner-process restart or main Git index write is performed.
+
+```powershell
+python docs/evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/run_check.py focused-final-headless res://tests/test_race_loading_optimisation.gd --headless
+python docs/evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/run_check.py effects-compat res://tests/test_runtime_loading_fixes.gd
+python docs/evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/run_check.py effects-mobile res://tests/test_runtime_loading_fixes.gd --renderer mobile
+python docs/evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/run_check.py interleaved-compat res://tests/profile_race_loading_optimisation.gd
+python docs/evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/run_check.py interleaved-mobile res://tests/profile_race_loading_optimisation.gd --renderer mobile
+python docs/evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/run_check.py first-lap-mobile res://tests/test_race_loading_first_lap.gd --renderer mobile --timeout 600 -- --first-emission
+python docs/evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/run_check.py compat-interruptions-final res://tests/test_race_loading_first_lap.gd -- --only-interruptions
+python docs/evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/run_check.py desert-old-loader-mobile res://tests/test_race_loading_first_lap.gd --renderer mobile --timeout 180 -- --first-emission --loading-control --theme=desert
+python docs/evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/summarize.py
+```
+
+The [raw evidence](evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/) includes controls, failures, all timing rows, images, source hashes, first-lap observations and command receipts. `python docs/evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/checkpoint.py` creates the [task-only patch](evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/task.patch); forward/reverse application and normalized content round trips pass in an owned directory, as recorded in the [checkpoint receipt](evidence/race-loading-implementation-2026-11-02/checkpoint.json). App/tracker baselines incorporate the concurrent authors' final changes and remove only this task's owned hunks, preventing those changes from entering the patch. No main Git index is written.
+
+The new diagnostics and fixture adaptations are separate from the six runtime source changes. Concurrent Daily/Forklift/Garage/startup/music work and build identities are preserved. Reload/rebuild, owner appearance/loading acceptance and representative Android memory, thermal, cold-start and input acceptance remain.
